spec sk11-materialised-conflict-value-preserving: 2 sessions, 20 permutations
# SK11, value-preserving arm (SET g.v = g.v). SK01 write skew, materialised: each transaction also writes the
# shared guard node g in the statement that takes its doctor off call. This is the
# documented snapshot-isolation remedy (Fekete et al., TODS 2005) for the absent
# locking read (G4).
# This arm writes g's CURRENT value back. The catalogue left its verdict unverified
# (G4); this transcript pins it.

starting permutation: s1r s1w s1c s2r s2w s2c
step s1r: MATCH (d:Doctor) WHERE d.oncall = true RETURN count(d) AS oncall
oncall
------
2     
(1 row)
step s1w: MATCH (d:Doctor {name:'alice'}) SET d.oncall = false WITH d MATCH (g:Guard {name:'g'}) SET g.v = g.v RETURN d.name AS who, g.v AS guard
who    |guard
-------+-----
"alice"|0    
(1 row)
